      "provenance": "literature_retrieved",
      "rationale": "[Literature audit 2026-11-05 (deliverome-analysis PR 236), verdict confirmed_exact: position confirmed at this residue. validation_level surface_and_function -> function_only (paper reports surface: not_reported, function: yes). Paper (PMID 42364996): \"we replaced the extracellular loop EL3 (residues 484-516) between TM11 and TM12 with a stable, short alpha-helix known as the ALFA tag (Fig. 1a).\". Audit note: Human SMVT; M483|P484 verified; this REPLACES 33 residues (484-516), not an insertion. Function: [3H]-biotin uptake in HEK293T retained with reduced efficiency (Kt 48.4 vs 72.3 uM; Vmax 1.3 vs WT). Surface NOT shown: NbALFA was bound to purified protein as a cryo-EM fiducial, not to intact cells. validation_level surface_and_function overstates; function only.] L1/L2/L3 all report the same SMVT_EM construct in which EL3 residues 484\u2013516 are replaced by the ALFA tag in the full-length, membrane-anchored protein. Python confirms residue 483 = M and residue 484 = P in the canonical 635-aa sequence, placing the N-terminal junction of the replacement at insert_after_residue = 483. The entire replaced segment and both flanking junctions fall within the EXTRACELLULAR span 477\u2013527, with adequate distance from both TM boundaries. The NbALFA binding assay on intact constructs constitutes direct surface-display validation, and normal expression was explicitly confirmed. Full-length human SMVT (SLC5A6) construct SMVT_EM in which the native EL3 segment (residues 484\u2013516) was replaced by the ALFA tag (PSRLEEELRRRLTEP); expressed in a heterologous system and probed with NbALFA nanobody on intact cells/particles to confirm extracellular surface display. The paper explicitly names residues 484\u2013516 as the replaced segment, placing the N-terminal junction of the tag at residue 483 (M) and the C-terminal junction at residue 517 (T). Both junctions lie within the EXTRACELLULAR span 477\u2013527, 7 residues from TM11 (ends 476) and 11 residues from TM12 (starts 528), well beyond the \u22653-residue TM-boundary requirement.",
